# [DD-13b.W23.3, D100] §2.22's ACCEPT HALF, and it is the half that says
# what the repair BOUGHT.
#
# §4.5 item 4's mechanism — the canonical pattern once as a `name`d
# definition, one block per regime whose pattern is a subroutine call —
# was MEASURED UNUSABLE for every pcrec-bench pattern id: a `(?&…)` call
# goes through PCRE2's own group-name grammar, which refuses `-` and `.`,
# and every id in all five bench sets is a hyphenated slug. The NAME
# grammar was widened for those ids and the CALL grammar cannot be (D26 —
# it is PCRE2's), so before the derived-identifier binding there was no
# spelling at all that reached a hyphenated definition.
#
# `(?&cls_upto_64)` reaches `name cls-upto-64` here. Without this fixture
# `derived_call_collision.rxtin`'s refusal is satisfied by a composer that
# binds nothing — a refusal fixture and its accept control are one
# instrument, not two.
#
# THE HYPHENATED SPELLING IS STILL REFUSED, and that is deliberate rather
# than a residual: `(?&cls-upto-64)` goes through PCRE2's grammar, which
# D26 makes PCRE2's rule and not one this format may widen.
#
# LEG A ONLY: legs B and C resolve no calls, and the instrument is
# `--source` (the composer) rather than `--list-source`.
target rx = caller

pattern [0-9][0-9]
name cls-upto-64

pattern ^(?&cls_upto_64)-(?&cls_upto_64)$
name caller
features recursion,named-groups
